WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:12.530
It seems Black Leg is onto us.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:15.490
Yeah, but a hacker who can't use a computer

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:18.500
is about as effective as someone 
with their hands and feet tied.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.460
See? Not using it isn't even an option.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.920
I'm in Nakasu now.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.850
Where do I go?

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.920
<i>Give us a second. He's on the move again.</i>

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.140
<b>Press button 
to cross</b>

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.140
Log in for a minute, then move...

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:38.600
He's putting up a fight, that's for sure.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.170
Even though he's trapped like a rat.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.090
Here we go. He's online again.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:49.070
<i>Irasawa, head for Nakasu-Kawabata Station.</i>

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:52.430
<i>Go in at exit 6 and to 
the end of the hallway.</i>

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.240
<i>He's in the restroom there.</i>

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.740
Chegaru-san, check it out.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.700
<b>Shadyjob.com</b>

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:00.700
<b>Important Notice

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.700
The site's under attack.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.370
Is it Black Leg?

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:07.170
He's probably trying to delete 
the post, but it's too late.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.800
<b>Occupied</b>

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:19.760
What is it?

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.470
I don't see anyone.

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:23.590
Was it a diversion?

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.270
But then, how was he hacking?

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:29.380
A virus?

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:30.650
What?

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:34.100
I get it! Impressive!

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.540
What are you talking about?

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:37.610
He set this all up.

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:42.120
He infected his own computer 
with a remote-access virus.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.020
Then he used home-brewed malware

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.540
to send it commands from 
a terminal on his phone.

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:25.490
<b>#08  Trick Play</b>

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.820
All right, it's back up.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:32.100
I'd better do something to get rid 
of all these bounty hunters...

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.310
<b>{Screen}Kanto Accent</b>

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.310
<b>Medium Build</b>

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.310
<b>I agree with the terms and conditions.</b>

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.310
<b>Publish</b>

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.320
Good luck with my next diversion.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.200
<b>Shadyjob.com</b>

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.200
<b>Looking For Someone (POW)!</b>

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:49.200
<b>Whoever brings this man in
will receive ten million yen</b>

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.050
I've got you now! That bounty is mine!

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:51.820
Wait, what?

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.830
The ten million is mine!

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.800
Get your ass back here!

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:02.220
<b>Banba Private Investigations</b>

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.000
I'm back.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.220
By yourself? Where's the mushroom?

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:04.540
He ran off somewhere.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.340
Said he had a plan.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:08.430
A plan?

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:10.390
{el: sign - take text from below}Regarding the celebrations,
I've made reservations
at that restaurant
on the national road.
The fun starts at 11 PM.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:12.460
It's him.

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:14.330
I got one, too.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.050
"Regarding the celebration,

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.860
I've made reservations at that 
restaurant on the National Road.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:21.360
The fun starts at 11 PM."

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.320
He even included a map.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:29.260
"Yamato did a good job stealing that base 
in the game at Gannosu the other day."

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:31.290
What's this supposed to mean?

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:34.180
Maybe he sent it to the wrong person?

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:38.740
No, but Yamato-kun didn't even 
manage to steal that base.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:40.250
Why would he...

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.050
I'll contact you if I need help.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.340
Yamato...  Stealing base...

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.470
<b>Yamato</b>

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.100
<b>Stealing Base</b>

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.930
<b>National Road</b>

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.930
National Road... 11 PM.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.930
<b>11 PM</b>

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:57.820
So Yamato's gonna be stealing something from 
somewhere on the National Road at 11 PM?

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.460
Probably from the location 
on the map he sent.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:02.150
Yamato... stealing?

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.790
Then it's obvious!

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:06.860
There's only one thing he steals 
outside of a baseball game.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:11.300
All right, we're in.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.780
Here's the log of his terminal.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.040
Let's see... "Thanks for the present.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:21.650
You said you'd treat me next 
time, right? I want barbecue."

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:24.860
Not the kind of message you'd usually
send in a situation like this...

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:26.010
Maybe it's a code?

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.220
Let's figure out what his trick is.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.620
Use his card info to find 
out what he's been—

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.360
Already on it.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.020
Here we go.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.480
Ten minutes ago, he bought a ticket 
for the bullet train over the internet.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:42.710
Leaving at 6:30 tomorrow 
morning, bound for Tokyo.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.690
I guess we can have Irasawa stake it out.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.700
Hang on.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.190
It's been updated.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:51.480
I see what he's trying to do.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:53.980
He bought a plane ticket, too.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.460
To Busan.

00:05:55.460 --> 00:05:57.370
Which one is the real one?

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.970
Or are they both fakes?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:04.130
I'd expect that kind of thing from him.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:07.800
Aw, he's shut down the terminal again.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.700
Can't you track him with the other 
active features on his phone?

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:16.150
Nope. He's probably using a 
smartphone case that cuts any signals.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.890
An anti-cracking measure....

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:21.650
But if he wants to play it like that...

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:24.650
Here come our security cameras.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:29.930
Let's see... He disappeared at the 
intersection near Haruyoshi earlier, so...

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:31.320
Most likely...

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.830
There he is!

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:34.580
That haircut is not subtle.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:36.370
What's his location?

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.080
Somewhere on the National Road.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:42.460
He probably thought hiding in the 
crowd would be safest option.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:47.840
Here you go.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:50.770
I grabbed it off him, just like you asked.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.350
I appreciate it, Yamato-kun.

00:06:53.350 --> 00:06:56.430
What the heck is going on, anyway?

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.540
Why have me pretend to be someone 
else and swipe Enokida's wallet?

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.500
Well, it's kinda complicated...

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:04.820
Oh, there's a note.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:09.070
Huh? What the hell is that mushroom thinking?

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.700
The terminal's receiving signals again.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:20.830
He might be waiting for contact from an ally.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.910
This is his third drink...

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:34.620
Is he just going to sit around killing time?

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.030
Most likely.

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:38.890
It's smarter than just running around blindly.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:45.240
We've finally got contact!

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:47.250
<i>Hey, it's me.</i>

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.940
<i>Everything's ready.</i>

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:51.220
<i>A friend of mine, a transporter,</i>

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:54.280
<i>can get you out of 
Hakata Port on a freighter.</i>

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.500
<i>I appreciate it.</i>

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:56.730
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:58.950
<i>I'll pick you up in 30 minutes.</i>

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.710
<i>Got it. I'll be in the usual family restaurant.</i>

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.210
What should we do?

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.960
Stake out Hakata Port?

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.110
No...

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:10.670
There's something about those emails...

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:14.780
One of them was a code, 
and he made contact using it?

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:18.370
I'm not quite convinced by that 
escape plan of his, either.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:21.790
In that case, since there's 
time before he leaves,

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:24.690
should we just rush him in the 
restaurant and kidnap him?

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.400
Inside a restaurant?

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:31.360
It'll be fine! Just gotta make 
sure no one notices, right?

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.430
<i>You ready to go, Irasawa?</i>

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:39.280
Yeah. Whenever you are.

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:40.580
Do it.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:45.470
A blackout?

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:47.130
Seriously?

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:03.490
It's finally back on...

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:05.440
I wonder what that was about.

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:07.330
Welcome.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:08.740
Party of one?

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:11.410
Nah, I'm supposed to be meeting someone...

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:14.390
I don't see him, though.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.690
Come on, you're done already?

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:33.760
Do you know how much a one-round 
KO pisses off the crowd?

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.850
Those homeless losers from 
before put up more of a fight!

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:38.800
A lot more!

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:48.900
Not even worth the effort...

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.870
Guess it's time to wrap this up.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.030
Tough luck.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:04.780
Just goes to show... Take computers away from 
hackers, and they're as weak as everyone else.

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:06.960
Die!

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.920
<b>PC Doctor's Factory</b>

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:19.380
<i>Not even worth the effort...</i>

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:22.890
<i>Guess it's time to wrap this up.</i>

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.590
<i>Tough luck.</i>

00:10:24.590 --> 00:10:29.250
<i>Just goes to show... Take computers away from 
hackers, and they're as weak as everyone else.</i>

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:30.400
<i>Die!</i>

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:34.440
Something wrong?

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.070
No... it's nothing.

00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:38.190
This case is closed.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:41.680
It took him until morning to finish up?

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:43.900
Maybe it was harder than he thought.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:46.700
He was probably just having 
fun messing with the kid.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.710
All that's left is to 
report in, and we're done.

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:52.330
A pretty sad end for Black Leg.

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.890
Were you waiting long?

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.280
You're here to report in, right?

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:06.390
"Black Leg has been eliminated."

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:08.560
Y-You're...

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.550
Stop right there.

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:12.550
No sudden moves, now.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:15.420
You're surrounded by Metro PD.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.900
How are you alive?

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.650
Because I'm not dead.

00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:26.080
The video you got was a fake.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.270
Here's the real one.

00:11:29.270 --> 00:11:30.940
<i>Tough luck.</i>

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:33.500
<i>Just goes to show... 
Take computers away from hackers...</i>

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.590
...and they're as weak as everyone else.

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:37.210
Die!

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:44.900
Tough luck. I'm not a hacker!

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:50.100
"Argh!"

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:56.270
The "me" you kidnapped? He had 
a different camera in his ring.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:00.370
i just had to add the screams later
to the video you received.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:02.570
All that stuff from after 
the camera tipped over.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:06.740
You must've really had faith in that 
Irasawa guy's assassination skills, huh?

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:10.770
Considering you were so sure I was dead 
just from the sound of my voice.

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:14.330
Who was that man disguised as you?

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:17.790
A hitman. An acquaintance of mine.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:20.660
Turns out we're about the same height,

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.760
so I asked him to fill in for me.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:26.720
I still say I'm a bit taller, though.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:30.930
Did you see the guy who crossed 
my path on the National Road?

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:35.650
I got the script into my 
buddies' hands through him.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:46.280
<b>Lin, put on clothes that 
conceal your face,
and wait at the family 
restaurant in Hirao.
Wait there for a bit.</b>

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:40.130
"Lin, put on clothes 
that conceal your face,

00:12:40.130 --> 00:12:41.990
and wait at the family restaurant in Hirao."

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.620
"Wait there for a bit."

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:52.200
<b>Banba. Once he's in position, call Enokida.</b>

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:51.550
"Banba. Once he's in position, call Enokida."

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.890
Everything after that went 
according to the script.

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:57.240
The part about me escaping 
on a freighter, I mean.

00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:58.920
After that, it was...

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:01.210
"Enokida hangs up."

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:04.380
<b>Enokida hangs up. He heads for the restroom.</b>

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:02.770
"He heads for the restroom."

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:07.860
"Lin, after waiting for a bit, 
also goes in there."

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:10.310
<b>Lin, after waiting for a bit, also goes in there.</b>

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.700
Move your ass over!

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:16.040
I can't go any further.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:17.520
It's hard to change like this!

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:23.440
<b>Enokida and Lin switch clothes and swap places.</b>

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:23.440
"Enokida and Lin switch 
clothes and swap places."

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.400
Don't forget this.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.800
Is this really gonna fool anyone?

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:33.620
All they have to go on 
is a broad description.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.080
The color of my clothes...

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:36.580
My hairstyle...

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:39.600
You'll find that sophisticated 
hi-tech types tend to fall

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:42.550
for the oldest tricks in the book.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:47.680
Oh, that looks pretty nice!

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:50.010
Here's the camera and transmitter.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:52.350
Keep those on you, no matter what.

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.350
We'll be right behind you.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:57.900
Then it was your group's turn.

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:02.480
Black Leg is abducted from the family 
restaurant under cover of darkness.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:06.440
<b>Banba heads to the family restaurant 
to rendezvous with Enokida.</b>

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:06.440
"Banba heads to the family restaurant 
to rendezvous with Enokida."

00:14:07.190 --> 00:14:08.650
I don't see him, though.

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:10.160
Banba-san!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.810
No wonder I didn't notice you.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.650
You look totally different from usual.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:18.070
How'd the plan go?

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:19.370
Smooth sailing so far.

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.840
All according to the script.

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:25.580
What is it?

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:28.300
I forgot that I left Saito-kun as a diversion.

00:14:28.560 --> 00:14:29.300
What?

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.720
He should be fine, though.

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:33.590
I sent help.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:38.100
Why does this keep happening to me?!

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:40.150
Get back here!

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:45.530
Say your pray—

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:53.230
H-Huh?

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:55.450
Would you be Saito-sama?

00:14:55.450 --> 00:15:00.420
I humbly apologize for the trouble 
my young master has caused you.

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:02.730
Young master?

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:05.590
Boy, oh, boy...

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:09.420
Looks like you didn't need our help.

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.900
Ew...

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:16.350
This asshole beat on me 
like he was having fun!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.570
I made sure he won't be
able to move for a while.

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:23.310
Now, once we know where his friends are...

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:27.980
He really is an ex-boxer. 
Guy sure can take a beating.

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.450
Had to really pull out all 
the stops to get him to talk.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:32.670
And those homeless guys?

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:34.840
Yep, that was him.

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:37.450
Seems he just did that for fun, though.

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:38.990
Did you get the password?

00:15:38.990 --> 00:15:40.510
Sure did.

00:15:40.510 --> 00:15:43.710
Here. I went ahead and unlocked it for you.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:47.870
So this person he's been emailing 
is the one he works for?

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:49.060
Most likely.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:50.340
What're you gonna do now?

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:55.610
Which brings us back to the video I sent you.

00:15:56.090 --> 00:16:00.370
The second you downloaded it,
I had all of your data.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:02.830
With my data-sniffing virus.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.240
Your "Flammulina"?

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:08.070
Yep. You know what that means, right?

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:12.240
It's a fungus. A mushroom with spores.

00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:14.660
And it spreads just like you'd expect...

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:17.830
Even to people who you've made contact with.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:21.660
The friend you were going to meet 
today? I have his data, too.

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:23.750
I got you all in one fell swoop.

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:27.230
Well, it's about time I got going.

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:30.880
I have a friend who's leaving town,
and I need to go see him off.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:36.380
And my job is finished. The rest is up to 
the Metro PD and the Cybercrime Unit.

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:38.430
I'm sure they'll give you a warm reception.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:44.550
Damn it.

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:53.900
Maybe I should ruin her life next.

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:58.240
You're an idol. You should 
really protect yourself better.

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:03.960
Why the hell would you keep pictures 
you don't want leaked on the Cloud?

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:04.620
<b>On</b>

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:04.790
<b>On a</b>

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:04.910
<b>On a totes</b>

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:05.080
<b>On a totes amaze</b>

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:05.210
<b>On a totes amaze date</b>

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:05.370
<b>On a totes amaze date with</b>

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:05.540
<b>On a totes amaze date with my</b>

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:05.670
<b>On a totes amaze date with my bae</b>

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.960
<b>On a totes amaze date with my bae <3</b>

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:10.940
Edits finished, upload complete!

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:13.470
You're having a lot of fun.

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:16.220
Wh-Who are you?! How'd you get in here?

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:19.140
Toying with people's lives...

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:22.680
Stop! S-Stay back!

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:34.860
You play, you pay.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:40.270
I doubt your life would be enough 
to cover what you owe, though.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:45.500
You really didn't need to see me off like this.

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:48.710
I know how to ride the bullet train.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:52.320
This might be the last time I see 
that crusty face of yours.

00:17:52.320 --> 00:17:53.620
It's a relief.

00:17:53.620 --> 00:17:56.170
You needn't feel so lonely without me, sir.

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:58.890
Are you going deaf?

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:02.220
Well, I guess nobody lives forever.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:03.810
Here you go.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.520
Some Hakata Torimon.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.100
Oh, my...

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:12.100
I feel as though my sleep will be somewhat
sounder, thanks to you, young master.

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:16.860
I didn't actually do anything. Your culprit 
went and got himself killed, remember?

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.310
Listen...

00:18:18.850 --> 00:18:20.500
Can I ask you something?

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:21.870
Of course.

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:25.790
Macro Hard had your boss's number.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:28.110
Call logs, email records...

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:30.700
He even had credit card records.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:32.760
Really?

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:34.610
Now, here's the odd thing...

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:36.800
Eight years ago, Matsuda Kazuo

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:40.730
bought a plane ticket to Fukuoka 
with his personal credit card.

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:47.270
What's up with that? Why would you 
buy the ticket under his name?

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:51.230
I suppose the statute of 
limitations has passed...

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:56.990
As I told you earlier, all was 
according to the master's orders.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.240
What does that mean?

00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:05.240
I was ordered by the master to help 
you escape and fake your death.

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:08.360
So the reason you didn't shoot me...

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:11.120
Yes, the master's orders, of course.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:12.580
That being said...

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:15.960
He also told me not to let you 
run off without taking a shot.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:19.890
And that you would be better off 
with some sort of discipline.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:23.800
When I reported back that your 
expression was akin to someone

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:25.760
who'd been shot with a BB gun,

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:28.520
he was overjoyed.

00:19:28.900 --> 00:19:30.190
What the hell?

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:33.440
Perhaps the two of you share 
the same fondness for pranks?

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:38.750
"That boy is sick. And there's 
no cure for what he has."

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:42.820
But there was more to what 
the master said that day...

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:48.080
That boy is sick. And there's 
no cure for what he has.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:51.540
I think the best thing to do is set him free.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:01.320
Would you like to visit sometime soon?

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:04.070
The master's birthday is coming up soon.

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:07.930
Hell no! I'm never going back to that place.

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:13.030
Well, in that case, please take care 
of yourself, Young Master Chihiro.

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:23.820
So who was the culprit, anyway?

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:27.030
Some hacker who was simply 
in it for the money, apparently.

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:32.540
A young man who is rather talented in this 
field, and who loves pranks, lent me a hand.

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.540
I see...

00:20:36.730 --> 00:20:37.960
What's the matter?

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:38.590
<b>Ma</b>

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:41.420
<b>Matsuda</b>

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:39.090
<b>Ka</b>

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:39.340
<b>Kazuo</b>

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.420
<b>Kazuo-sama</b>

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:41.420
What is it?

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:46.390
<b>Matsuda Kazuo-sama</b>

00:20:42.740 --> 00:20:46.390
<b>Happy</b>

00:20:43.650 --> 00:20:43.800
<b>B</b>

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:43.970
<b>Bi</b>

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:44.130
<b>Bir</b>

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:44.470
<b>Birt</b>

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:44.630
<b>Birth</b>

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:44.800
<b>Birthd</b>

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:45.130
<b>Birthda</b>

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:46.390
<b>Birthday</b>

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:49.690
That's right. It's today.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:56.690
That stupid son of mine...

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.270
Um... Master?

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:03.700
<b>You're the stupid one</b>

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:04.490
Yagi!

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:05.080
Sir?

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:08.160
I want you to check every nook 
and cranny of this room for bugs!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.370
<i>And get rid of this computer right now!</i>

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.610
What are you grinning about?

00:21:14.020 --> 00:21:15.080
Nothing much.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.990
Probably another stupid prank, right?

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:19.290
The meat's gonna get snatched up.

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:23.050
I went through hell 'cause 
of you, Enokida-san!

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:26.260
Who the heck was that old geezer?

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:28.660
Just a random acquaintance.

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:30.670
"Just an acquaintance," he says.

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:33.730
Sure as hell didn't seem that 
way to me, young master.

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:35.480
Wait, who's this "young master"?

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:37.610
Go on and eat, young master!

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:40.450
Shut up! I'm eating, okay?!

00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:44.420
You're picking up the check 
today, right, Maru-san?

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:47.530
Huh? I didn't hear anyone mention that.

00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:49.880
Hell, I might as well.

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:54.160
Since we're celebrating a family reunion.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.510
It's a treat? Lucky!

00:21:57.510 --> 00:21:59.290
All thanks to you, young master.

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:01.130
Thank you, young master.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:03.050
Seriously, who's this "young master"?

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:05.970
Oh, shut up!

00:23:04.180 --> 00:23:05.800
What's the real reason for doing this?

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:07.290
Kinda like a pinch hitter?

00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:08.060
Hit and run?

00:23:08.060 --> 00:23:09.160
The two of them work together!

00:23:09.160 --> 00:23:11.560
How does it feel to be betrayed?

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:13.260
Do you know where he is?

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:14.990
Where's my "Have a safe trip"?

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
#09  Hit and Run
